==Aspects==
[[File:MER-wall art-Giclee-Alduin.jpeg|Alduin and the Last Dragonborn|thumb|right]]
While it is a matter of debate if Alduin serves as a local variant of the likes of the Imperial Akatosh, the Khajiiti Alkosh, and the Elven [[Lore:Auriel|Auriel]] who govern time in the general sense, it can be inferred that Alduin governs the sphere of the End of Times giving him more definitive ties to aspects that share that duty.

===[[Lore:Alkhan|Alkhan]]===
To the Ancient [[Lore:Khajiit|Khajiit]], he is a Wandering Spirit known as '''Alkhan''', '''The Scaled Prince''', and the '''Firstborn of [[Lore:Akha|Akha]]'''. Texts that predate the [[Lore:Riddle'Thar|Riddle'Thar Epiphany]] claim that Alkhan was born when Akha bred with a demon of fire and shadow. Alkhan grew in size with each soul he ate, and ever hungered for the crown of [[Lore:Alkosh|Alkosh]]. He was slain by [[Lore:Lorkhaj|Lorkhaj]] and his companions, but will return one day along the Many Paths. Lorkhaj, [[Lore:Khenarthi|Khenarthi]], and Alkosh consider him to be an enemy.{{Ref|name=TWaS|{{Cite Book|The Wandering Spirits}}}}

===[[Lore:Thartaag|Thartaag]]===
The [[Lore:Skaal|Skaal]] recognize a version of the [[Lore:The Adversary|Adversary]] who will show up at the End of Seasons under the name '''Thartaag the World-Devourer'''.{{ref|name=ASS|{{Cite Book|Aevar Stone-Singer}}}}
===[[Lore:All-Maker|All-Maker]]===
In a claim that is seemingly at odds with the idea of Alduin being connected to the Skaal's malevolent Adversary, some sources instead postulate that the benevolent '''All-Maker''' of the Skaal is a distant echo of Alduin. The connection is made to highlight incredulity, however, and is not seriously proposed by the sources that suggest it.{{ref|name=TGATT|{{Cite Book|The Guardian and the Traitor}}}}

===[[Lore:Satakal|Satakal]]===
'''Satakal''' of the [[Lore:Yokuda|Yokudan]] pantheon shares aspects of, and is much like the Nordic Alduin, destroying one world to begin the next.{{ref|name=VOF|}}{{ref|name=EGTHammerfell|{{Cite Book|EGT|Hammerfell}}}} The two beings also share similar appellations, with Alduin being known as the First Dragon, and Satakal the '''First Wyrm''' and '''First Serpent'''.{{Ref|name=DFRaces|[[Daggerfall:Redguard|Redguard]] exclamations in ''[[Daggerfall:Daggerfall|Daggerfall]]''}}{{ref|name=SatakalSkinrazer|[[Online:Alik'r Desert Antiquities#Satakal Skinrazer|Satakal Skinrazer]] antiquity codex entry in [[Online:Online|ESO]]: ''[[Online:Greymoor|Greymoor]]''}}

===[[Lore:Atakota|Atakota]]===
The Argonian '''Atakota''' shares some traits with Alduin: each of its scales was a world that it devoured.{{ref|name=CotR|{{Cite Book|Children of the Root}}}}
{{NewLine}}

==Worship==
[[File:ON-furnishing-World-Eater Effigy.jpg|World-Eater Effigy|thumb|left]][[File:ON-polymorph-World-Eater's Living Armor.jpg|World Eater's Living Armor|thumb|right]]
For centuries, the followers, cultists and warriors of Alduin, the "First-Born" of the Dragons and the corruption of a dark prophecy, are said to have clashed with those of Akatosh, a terrible fight "within the family".{{ref|name=AvAC|[[Online:Akatosh vs. Alduin Crate|Akatosh vs. Alduin Crate]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} Some followers of ancient Nordic traditions thus adorn themselves with imagery of a clash between Akatosh and Alduin. Their markings symbolize that there must be balance in all things and that every story's beginning must come to its inevitable end, that there is no light without darkness, no fullness without hunger, and no life without death. These are thought to be the teachings of the great Dragons.{{ref|name=DFM|[[Online:Dragonclash Face Marking|Dragonclash Face Marking]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}{{ref|name=DBM|[[Online:Dragonclash Body Marking|Dragonclash Body Marking]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} The faithful also symbolize Akatosh and Alduin through twin orbs of sacred fire, one golden and one crimson, swirling around each other.{{ref|name=DFO|[[Online:Dragonclash Flame Orbs|Dragonclash Flame Orbs]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} According to the ''Song of Endings'', the faithful consider Alduin to be "but an appetite with wings" who consumes all, whether by fire or teeth.

Loyal followers of Alduin are said to worship at effigies surging with the World-Eater's power in order to gain illusory wings and the Eyes of Alduin.{{ref|name=WEE|[[Online:World-Eater Effigy|World-Eater Effigy]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} Dragon Cultists of Alduin gather during the [[Lore:Solstice (astronomy)|Winter Solstice]] in order to award new initiates with specially crafted stone piercings. Some claim Alduin's blood sometimes blesses the nose studs, turning them into rubies the shade of his eyes.{{ref|name=DCPiercings|[[Online:Dragon Cult Piercings|Dragon Cult Piercings]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} Dedicated followers of Alduin's cult are said to find both wisdom in the darkness his long shadow casts over Nirn, and a certain freedom in his hunger.{{ref|name=WEEyes|[[Online:World-Eater Eyes|World-Eater Eyes]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} They are known to perform customary fire dances, magically producing beautiful draconic images out of fire to accompany their ritual sacrifices.{{ref|name=WEFD|[[Online:World-Eater's Fire Dance|World-Eater's Fire Dance]] in the [[Online:Akatosh vs. Alduin Crate|Akatosh vs. Alduin Crate]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} A dramatic form of fiery [[Lore:Magical Transportation|teleportation]] is sometimes used by the faithful to announce their allegiance to the World-Eater.{{ref|name=WEFR|[[Online:World-Eater's Fiery Recall|World-Eater's Fiery Recall]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}

Faithful of Alduin are known to sometimes create [[Lore:Living Armor|Living Armor]] in honor of the deity. These smoldering [[Lore:Golem|golems]] of Nordic origin{{Ref|name=DL|[[ON:Dragonclash Living Armor Senche|Dragonclash Living Armor Senche]] mount description in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}} are given a razor sharp edge by Alduin's infamous hunger. They are created in dedication ceremonies which involve the faithful praying to Alduin to fuel the construct's power, so it may be filled with fire and rage, and bring its fury to bear against their enemies.{{Ref|name=ALAS}}{{ref|name=WELA|[[Online:World-Eater's Living Armor|World-Eater's Living Armor]] in [[Online:Online|ESO]]}}


