==Notes==
*Some scholars have speculated that a dragon's soul, once severed from its body, may simply dissolve over time or return to join [[Lore:Akatosh|Akatosh]]. Since Alduin's soul was not consumed by the Last Dragonborn despite his body being destroyed, this may help explain his ultimate fate.{{Ref|name=LADragons|}}
* A text by a Khajiit Moon-Priest transcribed by a scholar of the [[Lore:Mages Guild|Mages Guild]] suggests that Dragons, Clan Mothers of the [[Lore:Alkosh|Pride of Alkosh]], and [[Lore:Pridehome|Pridehome]] exist in some sense outside the tapestry of time and of linear progression, and so have always existed and will always exist, irrespective of what has occurred from the perspective of those bound by linear time. Consequently the "Doom to Come", the time when Dragons return to bring imbalance to the world, will also always exist.{{ref|name=Pridehome|{{Cite Book|Pridehome: A Place Outside Time?}}}}
*Alduin's Time-Eater title is shared by an individual known as Hungunthar Time-Eater who was said to have slayed the Kings of the East and conquered Dunkreath.{{ref|[[Skyrim:Slow Time#Word Walls|Slow Time]] word wall in ''[[Skyrim:Skyrim|Skyrim]]''}}
*Michael Kirkbride suggested that Alduin's downfall was possibly orchestrated by Akatosh, who time-schemed against his mirror brother to protect the current (and perhaps his favorite) Kalpa from being eaten.{{ref|name=MKpost|group=UOL|{{Cite Book|Michael Kirkbride's Posts|ns_base=GEN}}}}
*One of [[Lore:Ysgramor|Ysgramor's]] [[Lore:Five Hundred Companions|Companions]] was said to be Karkux the Tower of Meat, who even the [[Lore:Frost Giant|karstaag-men]] feared Alduin could not eat ever in whole.{{ref|name=500COTOYTR|group=UOL|{{Cite Book|The Five Hundred Mighty Companions or Thereabouts of Ysgramor the Returned|ns_base=GEN}}}}
* [[General:Adam Adamowicz|Adam Adamowicz]] and [[General:Jonah Lobe|Jonah Lobe]] designed Alduin's appearance in ''Skyrim'' by using the texture of [[Lore:Meteors|meteorites]] as a basis.{{Ref|name=JLP|group=UOL|{{Cite Book|Jonah Lobe's Posts|ns_base=GEN}}}}

